--TEST--
Each `new` of an undeclared class reports once, at the class name, and a method call, a property read and a return on the new object report nothing — `rule:types/one-mistake-reports-once`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Shop {
    // Each `new Undeclared()` gives one error. The method call, the property
    // read and the return give none.
    public static function label(): string {
        (new Undeclared())->open();
        string $name = (new Undeclared())->name;
        return (new Undeclared())->label();
    }
}
